                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <span style="font-size: 12pt;"><strong>Applicants who previously applied in response to Job Posting JC-423483 with the final filing date of 09/24/2024, must reapply to be considered for this recruitment.<br /><br /></strong><em><strong> 

Applications will be considered according to the established cut off periods of 11/13/24 and 12/24/24 candidates who are the most qualified will be invited to an interview. If a candidate for hire is identified during the established cut off period, candidates that file during the subsequent cut off period will not be considered.<br /><br />
</strong></em>
This position is located in the San Francisco Bay Peninsula, as such an additional 5% pay for Bay Area Engineer (Local 39 MOU) will be granted.
<br /><br />

Under the general direction of the Chief Engineer (CE) II, the Stationary Engineer inspects all heating and air conditioning equipment monthly in DMV state-owned offices; changes filters, belts, oil, and handles refrigerant; troubleshoots and repairs failed equipment independently with minimal supervision; follows safety procedures and lock out tag out. The incumbent also uses proper Personal Protective Equipment, and electrical safety procedures; ensures proper air flow and temperature control are maintained in the building; replaces worn and defective parts, including motors, compressors and condensers; purchases parts as needed; supervises repairs, trains managers on proper operations of equipment; performs minor plumbing, cleans clogged drains, replaces defective valves, washers in faucets, and repairs small water lines breaks or leaks; repairs and replaces worn and broken floor and ceiling tiles; repairs and replaces worn or defective locks; makes minor patches in cement to prevent injury; performs minor electrical repairs; replaces lights, light switches, ballasts, etc.; and writes correspondence and prepares reports.
<br /><br />
Desired qualifications: must be experienced in refrigerant recovery, evacuation, repair of refrigerant circuit components, and electrical troubleshooting.
<br /><br />
A hands on exercise may be conducted following the job interview.
<br /><br />
<strong>A CFC license is required.
<br /> </strong>
If you do not have list eligibility for the Stationary Engineer, you may take the online examination at&nbsp;</span><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"><a href="https://www.calcareers.ca.gov/JOBSGEN/0PBDA.PDF" style="text-decoration-line: none;"><span style="color: #0000ff; text-decoration-line: underline;">https://www.calcareers.ca.gov/JOBSGEN/0PBDA.PDF</span></a></span><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">.<br /> </span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> 

All eligible candidates may apply; however, hiring preference will be given to applicants who are currently permanent in the classification advertised applying through the Bargaining Unit 13 Post and Bid process. A training and development assignment may be considered. SROA/Surplus candidates are encouraged to apply.
<br /><br /> 
The position(s) being advertised may be subject to allocation approval by the Human Resources Branch. Fingerprint/Criminal Record Clearance is required before hire. The Salary Range shown is the minimum and maximum for a full-time appointment. Salaries for part-time and/or intermittent appointments may vary. Moving and relocation expenses will not be reimbursed for this position.
<br /><br /> 
